# Intake silence — freeze the ask clock

Silence nudge (3h) and resolve (36h) are measured from **when the question was asked**, not from `sms_conversations.updated_at`.

## Rule

| Source | When to use |
|---|---|
| `intake_state.open_question_asked_at` | Always prefer (via `resolveIntakeSilenceAskedAt`) |
| Recover from `intake_silence_nudge_sent_at − nudgeMs` | Legacy rows that were nudged without an ask stamp |
| `conversation.updated_at` | Last resort only — **persist into `open_question_asked_at` immediately** |

## Why

Sending a silence reminder (or any `saveState`) bumps `updated_at`. If silence is still measured from that field, the 36-hour resolve wait **restarts** and the request stays stuck on “already nudged.”

## Do

- Stamp `open_question_asked_at` when asking (`finishIntakeQuestion`)
- Persist derived ask time before outbound nudge SMS
- Use `resolveIntakeSilenceAskedAt` — do not read `updated_at` ad hoc

## Do not

- Use `row.updated_at` as the ongoing silence clock after a reminder
- Clear `open_question_asked_at` on nudge save
